  "body_html": "<h1>Solvable Game</h1>\n<p>A game is solvable if the set $S^\\infty$ of rationalizable outcomes is reduced to\na singleton:\n$$\n  S^\\infty=\\{s^*\\}.\n$$\nThis captures games whose common-rationality elimination process predicts a\nunique profile.</p>\n<h2>References</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>[MFoGT, Def. 4.4.3] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. A game is solvable if the rationalizable outcome set is a singleton.</li>\n<li>[MFoGT, Section 1.3.3] Laraki, Renault, and Sorin, <em>Mathematical Foundations of Game Theory</em>. Earlier use of solvability for iterated elimination.</li>\n</ul>",
